  "body": "Found while fixing #1357. That fix refuses a feed, arc or cycle with the spindle stopped (no `S.. M3` since the last `M5`) in `tormach.cps` only. The other spindle mill posts still post a cut with no spindle start, e.g. a stream that states no `SpindleSpeed`.\n\n**Why it was split off.** Every mill dialect's conformance golden (`crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`, `GOLDENS` x `POSTS`) is a bare legacy `.cl` stream with no tool and no spindle. Adding the rule to a dialect refuses all 13 of its goldens. So each dialect's goldens have to be posted from a dressed stream first, the way #1357 does for Tormach (`tests/common/legacy_program.rs`, `as_program`), and then regenerated. That is roughly 120 golden files across nine posts, plus the other suites that post bare legacy streams through these dialects.\n\n**Scope.** Spindle dialects only. Plasma, wire EDM and sinker EDM are exempt, and so is any machine with no spindle. A touch-probe section (a stated 0 rpm, #574) is exempt. Lathe posts already refuse feed-per-rev with no spindle speed.\n\n**Done means:** each spindle mill post refuses a feed, arc or canned cycle with the spindle stopped, by name. Its conformance goldens are posted via `as_program` and regenerated (listed in the PR). A pinning test per dialect fails with the rule reverted.\n\nPart of #1357's follow-up.\n",
